# Nuxt 3 Project Standards

This app uses **hybrid rendering**: `/` and `/feed` are SSR'd for crawlers; the rest of the app is a client-only SPA (`routeRules`). Stack: Nuxt 3 + Tailwind 4 + Zod + HttpOnly cookie auth + Bearer access in memory + `@nuxtjs/i18n` + `@nuxtjs/seo`. Runtime: **Node ≥ 24**. TypeScript: classic compiler pinned in `package.json` (required by `vue-tsc`; see below). As-built topology: [`implement/architecture.md`](../../implement/architecture.md).

## Toolchain compatibility & type safety

General principles — they apply to any dependency, not just today's versions:

* **Type-check is the gate.** `npx vue-tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` must pass before committing changes to `.vue` / `.ts` files. Never "fix" a failing check by skipping it, loosening `tsconfig`, or patching files inside `node_modules`.
* **Unit tests:** `npm test` (Vitest) for schemas, security helpers, rate-limit, and markdown sanitization — run after changing `server/schemas`, `server/utils/http.ts`, `server/rate-limit/`, or `renderPostBody`.
* **Upgrade tools together.** The type-checker, its compiler, and the framework plugins form one toolchain. Before bumping any of them (e.g. `typescript`, `vue-tsc`, i18n modules), confirm the new versions support each other — check release notes, then run the type-check to prove it. If a new major of a compiler/runtime is not yet supported by the surrounding tooling, stay on the latest supported line and note why in `package.json` history / docs.
* **Reproduce, don't assume.** When a tool crashes after a dependency change, verify whether it's a tooling break or a real code error by running the check with a known-good toolchain first. Fix real code errors immediately; roll back incompatible tool versions rather than working around them.
* **Follow library call signatures, not intuition.** When a typed API has overloads (i18n `t(...)`, DB `query<T>(...)`, etc.), match the library's documented parameter order and generic constraints; if the checker rejects a call, read the overload — do not cast or `any` it away. Prefer the library's own row/result types over hand-rolled shapes.
* **Docs follow the code.** When a compatibility constraint is discovered, record it in `implement/` (getting-started / architecture) so the next upgrade attempt sees it.
* **No suppressions.** Do not add `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`. Prefer fixing types or narrowing. Avoid new `any` except at a typed boundary that is immediately narrowed.

## Architecture

* **Modules:** public hub `/`, **Feed** `/feed`, **Time Management** `/tasks` (+ epics/analytics), **Chat** `/chat`. Do not assume every page requires login.
* **`pages/` / `components/`**: UI only. Extract data, multi-step flows, and shared state into `composables/`.
* **`composables/`**: Vue/Nuxt context (`ref`, `useState`, `useRoute`, `apiFetch`). Always pass an explicit key to `useState('unique-key', factory)`.
* **`utils/`** (client) / pure helpers: deterministic functions only — no `useNuxtApp()`, `useRoute()`, or `useRuntimeConfig()` at module top level.
* **`server/api/`**: Thin handlers. Auth → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → domain `server/db` or `server/services` → return JSON or `mapDomainError`.
* **`server/schemas/`**: Shared Zod request schemas — add new body/query shapes here first; reuse create/update fragments instead of duplicating fields.
* **`server/services/`**: Multi-step workflows only (task save, timer start/stop, post create/update/share, auth signup/refresh/reset, chat send, admin role policy, upload persist after multipart parse) — not every CRUD route.
* **`server/db/`**: SQL / persistence (barrel via `server/utils/db.ts`). Keep business orchestration out of DB modules when a service already owns the workflow. Prefer splitting a DB module before it exceeds ~500 lines (e.g. read / write / social).
* **`server/utils/`**: auth, cookies, http helpers, mailer, R2, cache, queue — not a second home for domain SQL.
* **`types/`**: Shared DTOs used by both client and server (`types/task.ts`, `types/post.ts`, `types/story.ts`, `types/chat.ts`, `types/locale.ts`).
* **Feed → Tasks:** use `usePlanPostAsTask` — do not call `useTasks` directly from feed presentation components for "plan as task".

### File size / decomposition triggers

Split or extract when any of these hold (review, don't force a big-bang rewrite):

* Vue SFC ≳ **400** lines, or `<script setup>` ≳ **200** lines
* `server/db/*.ts` ≳ **500** lines
* Two composers / editors share audience, attachment, style, or submit logic → shared composable / child components
* A page owns fetch + charts + CRUD + dialogs → extract composables and presentational children

Prefer domain-named children (`PostReactionBar`, `FeedCategoryFilter`, `useVoiceRecorder`) over generic `utils.vue`.

## Data fetching & auth (client)

* Authenticated API calls: use `apiFetch` from `useApi()` — not raw `$fetch` (attaches Bearer, `credentials: 'include'`, refresh-on-401).
* `$fetch` with `credentials: 'include'` is OK for auth bootstrap endpoints (`login` / `signup` / `refresh` / `logout` / `verify-email` / `forgot-password` / `reset-password`) from `useAuth` only — document any new exception next to the call.
* **Multipart uploads:** use `apiFetch` with a `FormData` body. Do **not** set `Content-Type` manually. `apiFetch` skips in-flight coalescing for `FormData` so parallel uploads do not share responses. Identical in-flight GETs (same method + url + query) share one promise; do not reintroduce a fixed delay throttle on the first request.
* **Never** persist refresh tokens in `localStorage`. Access token is in-memory; cookies are HttpOnly (`mgmt_rt`, `mgmt_at`).
* Client guard: `middleware/auth.global.ts` — public `/`, `/feed`, auth forms; protect `/tasks`, `/chat`, settings, admin, …
* Server: `requireUser` / `requireAdmin` / `requireSuperAdmin`; feed list/detail GETs may use `getOptionalUser`.
* Media: same-origin `/api/uploads/*` uses `mgmt_at` cookie — avoid new `?access_token=` URLs.
* Do not introduce Pinia unless necessary; follow existing composable stores (`useAuth`, `useTasks`, `usePosts`, `useChat`, …).
* API errors: prefer `apiErrorMessage(err, fallback)` from `~/utils/apiErrorMessage` over ad-hoc `data.statusMessage` casts.

## Nitro API handlers

```ts
// ✅ validate → auth → service or db
import { parseBody, mapDomainError } from "~/server/utils/http"
import { taskUpsertBodySchema } from "~/server/schemas"

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const user = requireUser(event)
  try {
    const body = await parseBody(event, taskUpsertBodySchema)
    return await saveTaskForUser(user.sub, body)
  } catch (err) {
    mapDomainError(err)
  }
})
```

* Prefer `parseBody` / `parseQuery` from `~/server/utils/http.ts` with schemas from `~/server/schemas`.
* Use `requireUser` / `requireAdmin` from `~/server/utils/authContext` — do not re-parse JWT in each route.
* Integer enums (`status`, `priority`, `role`, message `kind`, …) must be numbers on the wire — reject strings with `400`.
* Prefer semantic status codes: `400` validation, `401` unauthenticated, `403` forbidden, `404` missing, `500` unexpected.
* Never log passwords, tokens, verify/reset URLs, or raw Authorization headers. On queue/mail failures, log the error only — not the one-time link.
* Prefer `DomainError` + `mapDomainError` over `Object.assign(new Error(...), { statusCode })` in new code.
* **Multipart exception:** upload routes use `readMultipartFormData` + shared `uploadPolicy` / magic-byte checks — not `parseBody`. Keep transport parsing in the handler; move validated persistence to a service when the flow spans policy + DB + R2.

## Rate limiting

* Module: `server/rate-limit/` (policies, keying, store, check). Middleware: `server/middleware/rate-limit.ts`.
* Import from `~/server/rate-limit` — do not reintroduce a `server/utils/rateLimit` shim.
* Counters are **in-memory / per process**. Do not assume Redis-backed rate limits; Redis is for the cache facade only (`REDIS_URL`). Multi-instance deploys need a distributed atomic store before raising traffic assumptions.
* Client IP uses `X-Forwarded-For` — only safe behind a trusted proxy. Document proxy trust when changing `clientIp`.
* When changing policies or keying, extend `tests/rate-limit.test.ts` (scope, window, prefix matching).

## Cache, Redis, and queue

* Cache facade: `server/utils/cache.ts` (memory default; Redis when `REDIS_URL` is set; fail-open).
* Do not call Redis clients outside the cache infrastructure.
* Mutations that affect cached public reads must invalidate via the existing cache-bust helpers / `cache.invalidate` jobs — see [`implement/cache-queue.md`](../../implement/cache-queue.md).
* Background work (email, cache bust) goes through MySQL `jobs` + `server/plugins/job-worker.ts` — do not await SMTP inline on request paths.

## Chat

* Spec / as-built: [`implement/chat-spec.md`](../../implement/chat-spec.md), [`implement/api.md`](../../implement/api.md).
* Routes under `/api/chat/*`; DB in `server/db/chat.ts`; UI `/chat` + `useChat` + `plugins/chat-inbox.client.ts`.
* Message kinds are **integer enums** (`ChatMessageKind`). Validate with shared Zod schemas.
* Participant ACL on every conversation/message route — never trust client-supplied peer ids without membership checks.
* Media (image / voice) uses the same upload pipeline as Feed (`uploads` + R2). Composer must clean up `MediaRecorder` streams and object URLs on unmount.
* Thread live updates: SSE on `/api/chat/conversations/:id/stream` while a conversation is open — do not reintroduce a fixed 3.5s message poll. Keep a slow REST `?after=` fallback only when the stream is down. Connection state for the thread EventSource must be **module-scoped** (shared across `useChat()` callers: page + inbox plugin). Catch up with `?after=` on every SSE `ready`. Inbox badge uses `/api/chat/inbox/stream`. Clear EventSource / timers on sign-out / leave `/chat`.
* Unread totals and per-conversation `unreadCount` come from denormalized `chat_conversation_reads.unread_count` (migration `0015`); send/read must keep counters in sync.
* Read receipts: prefer server projection (`readByPeer` / `peerLastReadAt`); keep any client helper pure and shared if both sides need the same math.

## Manuscript & post editing

* Formats: `update` (short) vs `manuscript` (long). Body ceilings: `POST_BODY_MAX_UPDATE` / `POST_BODY_MAX_MANUSCRIPT` via `postBodyMaxForFormat` — do not reintroduce deprecated short/long aliases.
* Edit desk: `/feed/edit/:id`. Format is **fixed** after create; validate with shared schemas / service logic.
* Manuscripts carry `contentLocale` + optional `translationGroupId` / `translations`. Preserve translation-group invariants when creating locale variants.
* Prefer shared editor pieces between `PostComposer` and `ManuscriptStudio` (audience, attachments, font/color maps from `~/types/post`) instead of copying conditional CSS maps.
* Load Source Serif 4 via `useManuscriptFont()` (deferred stylesheet) — do not add a render-blocking Google Fonts `<link rel="stylesheet">` on Feed / write / edit.
* Lazy-load heavy editor UI when it is not on the critical path.

## ConfirmDialog & destructive actions

* Use `ConfirmDialog` (or the same accessible pattern) for destructive confirms — not native `confirm()` / `prompt()` for product UI.
* Requirements: focus trap + restore, Escape / backdrop dismiss where appropriate, busy/disabled while the mutation runs, clear confirm vs cancel labels, no accidental double-submit.
* Non-destructive prompts (e.g. rename) should still use an accessible dialog, not `window.prompt`.

## UI / UX (practical)

* Loading: use existing `SkeletonBlock` / `SkeletonList` (or matching pulse placeholders) — avoid blank flashes.
* Mutations: give immediate feedback (toast via `useToasts`, disabled/pending buttons). Optimistic UI + rollback for toggles (like/reaction) when already patterned that way.
* Risky subtrees: wrap with `<NuxtErrorBoundary>` when isolation matters (see feed).
* Images: set `width` / `height` (or fixed aspect) to limit CLS. No `@nuxt/image` in this project — native `<img>` / media is fine.
* Theme: respect `data-theme` + existing slate/brand utilities; do not invent a parallel token system (`bg-background`, etc.).
* Motion: 150–300ms; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
* a11y: visible labels, keyboard focus rings, meaningful `statusMessage` / inline errors on forms.
* Page titles: `useSeoMeta({ title })` on pages that need a distinct document title.
* Browser resources: always tear down intervals, `MediaRecorder`, object URLs, and document-level listeners in `onBeforeUnmount` / route leave.

## Performance (SPA-aware)

* Lazy-load heavy / conditional UI: `<Lazy*>` or `defineAsyncComponent` for modals, charts, story viewer, manuscript studio.
* Browser-only APIs (`window`, `localStorage`): guard with `import.meta.client`. On SSR'd public routes, auth chrome must use `isAuthenticatedUi` / `userUi` (ready after mount) so hydration matches the guest HTML. Only non-secret prefs and profile chrome go in `localStorage` — not tokens.
* Keep Chart.js and large editors out of the initial critical path when possible.

## Dead code & deprecations

* Remove unused routes, composable exports, and compatibility shims in the same change that replaces them (or a fast follow).
* Do not leave `@deprecated` aliases indefinitely once callers are gone.
* Prefer deleting legacy endpoints (e.g. old `/like` helpers) once reactions cover the behavior — update `implement/api.md` in the same PR.

## i18n

Full as-built flow: [`implement/i18n.md`](../../implement/i18n.md).

* **Locales:** `en` (default), `vi`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`. Messages live in `i18n/locales/*.json` (Nuxt i18n v10 `restructureDir`).
* **Routing:** `strategy: 'no_prefix'` — no `/en/...` paths. Switch with `LanguageSwitcher` (Settings → Language, or header account menu).
* **Persistence:** `useSettings().locale` in `mgmt:settings:v1`. `plugins/i18n-locale.client.ts` syncs settings ↔ `setLocale` ↔ Day.js locale ↔ `html[lang]`. Cookie `mgmt_locale` is only for first-visit browser detection.
* **Usage:** `$t` / `useI18n().t` for chrome, toasts, SEO titles. Add every new key to **all four** locale files (`en` first). Escape literal `@` as `{'@'}`.
* **Plurals:** with named interpolation use `t(key, { count }, count)` — named object second, plural number third (the overload order vue-i18n defines).
* **Labels:** `STATUS_I18N_KEYS` / `ROLE_I18N_KEYS` / `PRIORITY_I18N_KEYS` / `RECURRENCE_I18N_KEYS` from `~/types/task` + `t(...)`. Seeded post categories: `CATEGORY_I18N_KEYS` + `categoryDisplayName` from `~/utils/categoryLabel` (DB `name` fallback for custom dirs). Dates: Day.js after locale sync, or `INTL_LOCALE` from `~/types/locale`.
* Do **not** invent a parallel i18n stack, store locale on the user row, or hardcode English UI strings in new UI. User-authored content stays untranslated.

## SEO

* Site identity / robots / sitemap live in `nuxt.config.ts` (`@nuxtjs/seo`, `site.url = https://dntechx.com`). Do not invent a second SEO stack.
* Keep private app routes out of the sitemap; page titles stay on `useSeoMeta` + `t('seo.*')`.
* Dynamic OG image generation is intentionally off (`ogImage.enabled: false`) on this host.
